            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Hải Sản Thuận Kiều 2 - An Thới (CN2)",
            "review_text": "Flyer302997\nTokyo, Japan11 contributions\n0\nCooking is hard to come by, wrong things arrive\nDec 2025 • Family\nIt's a Chinese seafood restaurant, and Vietnamese dishes like pho and spring rolls aren't on the menu.\n\nI had trouble getting the food I ordered, so I waited 20 minutes for the first dish to come and a total of over 30 minutes for the rest of the menu.\nThey don't seem to know which table the finished dish is on because the staff gather to check which table it is on.\nHe said he was sorry, so maybe our family just happened to be late.\n\nI ordered orange juice with no ice for my kids, and they brought me orange juice with ice, and I told them no ice, but then I got orange juice with ice again, and I ended up getting orange juice with ice three times. In addition, the number of orders was also accounted for at double.\n\nThe taste was light and not remarkable, but the steamed shrimp was delicious.\n\nIt is recommended for those who have plenty of time because there are times when orders have not been made and who are tired of Vietnamese food.\nAlso, at the checkout, check the menu name (receipt is in Vietnamese, so be careful) and the number. They fix it correctly and apologize.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten December 27, 2025",
